costeroids like prednisone. As with other antibiotics, 克拉霉素 can disrupt gut flora, leading to life-threatening pseudomembranous colitis caused by Clostridioides difficile. These findings underscore its risk profile beyond typical antibiotic side effects [Data: Relationships (9073, 9094, 9066, 9097); Entities (15705, 16758, 15464, 16828)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"克拉霉素 is contraindicated in specific high-risk patient populations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"克拉霉素 is explicitly contraindicated for patients with 低钾/镁血症 and 缺血性心脏疾病 due to the heightened risk of QT interval prolongation and associated cardiac events. Although direct evidence linking 克拉霉素 to liver impairment is not listed in the provided data, it shares metabolic pathways with drugs like 伏立康唑—known to accumulate in 肝功能受损患者—suggesting caution is warranted. The contraindicication in electrolyte-imbalanced and cardiac-compromised patients reflects regulatory and clinical guidance aimed at preventing lethal arrhythmias [Data: Relationships (5634, 5639); Entities (14446, 1845)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"克拉霉素 affects key pharmacokinetic indicators like AUC and cortisol levels\",\n            \"explanation\": \"克拉霉素 significantly alters pharmacokinetic parameters of co-administered drugs by inhibiting CYP3A4 and P-glycoprotein. This results in increased AUC (area under the curve) for drugs such as corticosteroids, raising their systemic exposure and toxicity risk. Specifically, 克拉霉素 has been shown to elevate 皮质醇水平 suppression when combined with glucocorticoids, necessitating monitoring during therapy initiation or discontinuation. These effects demonstrate 克拉霉素’s broad influence on drug metabolism and endocrine indicators, reinforcing the need for therapeutic drug monitoring [Data: Relationships (849, 857); Entities (13683)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cross-reactivity risks include both allergy and antimicrobial resistance\",